### Normalized scores (1–100)

**Tool use: 93/100.** Estimated based on rank #7/214 on AI Intelligence Index and similar-tier models. Caps: top-tier agentic capabilities.

**Reasoning: 92/100.** Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index: 53 (rank #7/214). GDPval-AA and HLE benchmarks not publicly scored. Comparison: Claude Opus 5.5 (58, rank #1), Gemini 4 Argon (53, rank #8). Caps: strong reasoning but not top-of-class; similar to Gemini 4 Argon.

**Context window: 100/100.** 1M tokens measured. Caps: highest among evaluated models at this tier; enables longest document processing and complex RAG.

**Multimodal: 100/100.** Text + image input, text output. 1M context supports documents and images. Caps: standard full multimodal for frontier models.

**Coding: 95/100.** Estimated based on OpenAI's strong coding reputation and rank #7/214 on AI Intelligence Index. Caps: excellent coding capabilities; likely competitive with Claude Opus 5.5 on coding tasks.

**Cost efficiency: 40/100.** $10/M input, $50/M output. $3.26 per Intelligence Index task. Very expensive per token. 60M tokens from Intelligence Index (rank #45/115) — fairly concise. Caps: poor cost-efficiency; only viable for budget unconstrained workloads.

**Overall Score: 88/100.** Mean of Tool (93) + Reasoning (92) + Context (100) + Multimodal (100) + Coding (95) = 95.8. High-performance reasoning and coding model, but extremely expensive; best for budget-unconstrained critical work.

